# Sword of Extermination blade, exported from ~/Blender/SOE.blend (Blender 5.3).
#
# The model is authored pointing straight DOWN: the tip is at -Y, the handle end at +Y,
# the blade's flat faces look along +-X and its width runs along Z. That is Blender's
# own -Z up axis converted to OBJ's Y-up by the standard NEGATIVE_Z/Y export, so no
# extra rotation is baked in here -- what points down in Blender points down in game.
# Base (handle end) is +4.147, tip is -4.909, so the mesh is 9.056 units long; the
# renderer centres it and moves it by -height/2 to hang the blade from its base.
# UVs are the author's, occupying u 0.53..0.70, v 0.47..0.72 of soe_blade.png.
# Normals are deliberately absent: ObjMesh derives a flat one per triangle, which is
# what faceted steel wants, and keeps this file in the same shape it always was.
